ld military  titles positions and ranks including  that of vice admiral of the royal navy  in windsor brits are standing by the  queen i think the queen will rise above  it she's she's uh  you know she's been around for a very  long time and she's an extremely wise  and sensible lady  now this is not the first royal scandal  but it does hit close to home it's the  first time the queen has had to take  such action against one of her own sons  crystal gamson global news london  ahead a landmark war crimes verdict  against a former syrian officer  there is a landmark court verdict in a  war crimes case involving syrians who  suffered abuse or lost relatives at the  hands of bashar al-assad's regime a  german court sentenced a former syrian  colonel to life in prison for crimes  against humanity anwar raslan is linked  to the torture of at least 4 000 people  at a prison outside of damascus a decade  ago it is the first ever conviction on  charges of state-backed torture  committed during syria's civil war  it's a recognition of the crimes  committed in syria so i hope that this  sentence and this verdict will be  a strong pace for future work  raslan denied the allegations against  him he fled syria in 2012 and went to  germany where police began investigating  his background survivors of torture in  syria have had limited options for  justice western powers have tried to  refer cases to the international  criminal court but those attempts have  been blocked by russia and china it's  hoped this case will be a blueprint for  future prosecutions  spuds of kindness next to quebec man  chips in big to help prince edward  island  so this is henrietta an adventurous pet  chicken who flew the coop in dramatic  fashion last weekend henrietta lives in  the garage of a nova scotia plumbing  business and snuck onto a truck as a  stowaway not the first time she's done  that they say she likes to travel she  made it to a town about 10 minutes away  and was found wandering the streets and  was taken in by a wildlife shelter  henrietta has since made the trip back  home safe and sound  well we could all use some more  uplifting news these days so tonight we  leave you with a story about making the  best of a tough situation it involves  pei potatoes and one man's effort to  help solve two problems at once here's  mike armstrong  yeah they are a staple in fact potatoes  are about as basic a staple as they get  sam watts goes through a lot of them and  thankfully right now has a lot of them  watts runs the welcome hall mission in  montreal its food bank helps about 2 500  people a week add to that the hundreds  and hundreds it feeds every day in our  kitchens we're making about 7 000 meals  every week  that can use up a lot of potatoes now  the fact watts warehouse is fully  stocked with potatoes is thanks to a  donation by this man mack watson is a  retired geologist who wanted to help the  twist is it wasn't the mission that was  the inspiration in the middle of night  one about about three weeks ago  i  had this idea  watson had been following news of the  situation in pei after two cases of a  potato fungus were found in october  ottawa banned exports to the u.s pei  potato farmers had just had one of their  best years in memory and are now looking  at huge losses it's extremely tough  we've all lost a bit our ambition our  our love for what we do farmer robin  stein says he may have to destroy as  much as 70 percent of his crop  province-wide about 120 million dollars  worth of potatoes can't go to market it  was stein who sold the trailer load to  the montreal mission it was only a drop  in the bucket  but one he appreciates  it was a wonderful thing to be a part of  people outside the province are are  thinking about watson says there was a  message in what he did he wanted the  farmers to know the rest of the country  cares well pei wasn't the only place  that heard that message the mission says  it's already gotten calls from people  wanting to donate and other missions in  the country looking for help setting up  something similar  mike armstrong global news montreal  and that is global national for this  thursday i'm donna friesen tonight's  your canada is okanagan lake near  kelowna bc we'd love to see your canada  please email it to viewers at  globalnational.com thanks for watching  and hope to see you here again tomorrow  take care of yourselves bye-bye  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

